Vikram and Betal: The Lost Necklace

King Vikram was carrying Betal through the forest once again.

Betal began his story.

“Once there was a queen who lost her precious necklace,” said Betal. “She was very upset.”

The king ordered all the servants to find it.

But no one could find the necklace.

A clever minister came forward and said, “Your Majesty, I have a plan to find the thief.”

He gathered all the servants and gave each of them a stick.

He said, “These are magic sticks. The thief’s stick will grow longer by morning.”

All the servants took their sticks home.

The thief became scared and thought, “If my stick grows, I will be caught!”

So he cut his stick shorter.

The next day, all the servants returned.

The minister checked the sticks and found one shorter than the others.

He pointed to the servant and said, “You are the thief.”

The servant confessed.

Betal then asked, “Vikram, how was the thief caught?”

Vikram replied, “Because fear made him reveal himself.”

As soon as Vikram spoke, Betal flew back to the tree.

💖 Moral:

Fear can reveal the truth.
